{"ts": "2026-11-27T00:32:22.281329Z", "run_id": "r-20261127T0031Z-32a3", "unit": "openspec:agent-roles-and-ownership", "seq": 16, "type": "delegate.result", "question": "Q-001", "id": "Q-001", "status": "answered", "reason": "The question treats two scenarios from different capabilities as mutually exclusive, but they assert different definitions of one shared schema file. I verified in the repository that the grant-expiry additions (grantor_id in the two permission definitions, grant_expired in ev_token_denied) are already present at the base, and that the schema has the $defs / oneOf / discriminator.mapping structure design.md D6 says each new event type extends. Adding the two new definitions does not touch the three existing ones, so both THENs can be true simultaneously. No spec deletion is needed.", "called": true, "tasks": ["1.1", "2.1", "3.1", "3.2", "4.1", "5.1"], "target": null, "kind": "ambiguous", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code", "cost_usd": 0.82552625, "decision": "answer", "answer_sha256": "4019c6d3eaed0621d17ab66690d42a706957c9bf7b69d128a54f7f03f3d0d5f5", "checked": [{"ref": "openspec/specs/grant-expiry/spec.md:256", "quote": "SHALL add to the payload of `ev_agent_permission_granted`", "claim": "The grant-expiry scenario concerns the existing permission-granted, permission-revoked and token-denied definitions, not the two new ones this unit adds."}, {"ref": "openspec/specs/grant-expiry/spec.md:263", "quote": "the three definitions list those properties and that enum value, and the `required` lists they had are", "claim": "Its THEN asserts only properties and an enum value of three existing definitions and that their required lists are unchanged."}, {"ref": "spec:specs/agent-roles-and-ownership/spec.md#scenario-the-contract-lists-both-events", "quote": "both definitions exist with exactly those payload property names, the two types are keys of", "claim": "This unit's THEN asserts only the two new definitions, their mapping keys and their oneOf refs."}, {"ref": "docs/architecture/contracts/events/audit-event.schema.json:1064", "quote": "\"ev_agent_permission_granted\": {", "claim": "The permission-granted definition grant-expiry refers to already exists in the schema at the base."}, {"ref": "docs/architecture/contracts/events/audit-event.schema.json:1180", "quote": "\"grantor_id\": {", "claim": "The grantor_id property grant-expiry added is already present, so that scenario is satisfied at the base."}, {"ref": "docs/architecture/contracts/events/audit-event.schema.json:1371", "quote": "\"grant_expired\",", "claim": "The grant_expired enum value grant-expiry added to ev_token_denied is already present."}, {"ref": "docs/architecture/contracts/events/audit-event.schema.json:3211", "quote": "\"discriminator\": {", "claim": "The schema has the top-level discriminator whose mapping this unit extends with two new keys."}, {"ref": "spec:design.md", "quote": "The audit contract has one definition per event type under `$defs`", "claim": "Design D6 says each new event type adds a $defs definition, a oneOf entry and a mapping entry, which touches nothing grant-expiry asserted."}]}
